---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="machine-learning"
  title="DBSCAN"
  description="Density-based clustering that needs no k. It grows clusters wherever points are packed tightly, follows whatever shape they take, and labels the sparse leftovers as noise. Watch it flood-fill your own blobs in the first view, then open the second one, where the three relations the algorithm is actually built on (directly reachable, reachable through a chain, and connected) are worked out on small cases you can read point by point."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="db" width="600" height="600"></canvas>
      <canvas id="rc" width="900" height="640" hidden></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div class="control">
        <label>View</label>
        <div class="seg" id="mode">
          <button data-m="clusters" class="active">Clusters</button>
          <button data-m="reach">Reachability</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="cl-controls">
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <button class="btn" id="run">Run</button>
          <button class="btn ghost" id="step">Step</button>
          <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Restart</button>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <button class="btn ghost" id="regen">Random points</button>
          <button class="btn ghost" id="clear">Clear</button>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label>Random data</label>
          <div class="seg" id="data">
            <button data-d="moons" class="active">Moons</button>
            <button data-d="blobs">Blobs</button>
            <button data-d="noise">Blobs + noise</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="rc-controls" hidden>
        <div class="control">
          <label>Case</label>
          <div class="seg" id="rcase">
            <button data-c="0" class="active">Both ways</button>
            <button data-c="1">One way</button>
            <button data-c="2">Blocked</button>
            <button data-c="3">Two borders</button>
            <button data-c="4">Noise</button>
            <button data-c="5">Not core</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Neighborhood ε <b id="epsval">42</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="eps" min="12" max="90" value="42" />
      </div>
      <div class="control">
        <label>Min points <b id="mpval">5</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="mp" min="2" max="12" value="5" />
      </div>

      <div class="readout" id="cl-readout">
        <div class="row"><span>Clusters found</span><b id="nclust">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Noise points</span><b id="nnoise">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <div class="readout" id="rc-readout" hidden>
        <div class="row"><span>p is</span><b id="pkind">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>q is</span><b id="qkind">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Same cluster</span><b id="samec">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Next click sets</span><b id="nextsel">q</b></div>
      </div>

      <p class="note" id="note">
        Click the canvas to add points. Restart, then Step, to watch clusters
        flood outward from dense cores.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Hit <b>Restart</b> then <b>Step</b>. DBSCAN picks a dense point and
      <b>floods outward</b> through neighbors within ε, so a cluster takes on
      whatever shape the data has, even a long crescent.
    </li>
    <li>
      Grey points are <b>noise</b>: they never gather enough ε-neighbors to join
      anyone. Built-in outlier detection, for free.
    </li>
    <li>
      The two knobs fight each other. Too small an <b>ε</b> (or too high
      <b>min points</b>) shatters everything into noise; too large and separate
      clusters <b>merge</b>. The right density sits in between.
    </li>
    <li>
      Open the <b>Reachability</b> view. Everything above rests on three
      relations: q is <b>directly reachable</b> from p when p is a core and q
      lies within ε of it; q is <b>reachable</b> from p when a chain of such
      steps gets there, every point along the way being a core; and p and q are
      <b>connected</b> when some one core reaches both.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>One way</b> is the case to sit with. A core reaches the border point on
      its fringe, but the border point reaches nothing at all, because the
      definition asks the point you leave <b>from</b> to be a core. Reachability
      is not symmetric, and the whole rest of DBSCAN is arranged around that.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Blocked</b> shows what a border point cannot do. It is reached from the
      left cluster, and a point of the right cluster sits within ε of it, yet
      the chain <b>stops</b> there: a hop may only leave a core. Two clusters
      stay two, and the border point simply joins whichever was found first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Two borders</b> is why clusters are defined by connectivity and not by
      reachability. Neither border reaches the other, in either direction, and
      they still belong to the same cluster, because one core in the middle
      reaches both. Drop the connectivity requirement and a cluster would stop
      being a single set.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Not core</b> is the trap. The two points sit well within ε of each
      other, and still nothing holds between them: neither is a core, so no
      relation can start anywhere. <b>Being close is not the same as being
      reachable.</b>
    </li>
    <li>
      In any case, drag <b>ε</b> or <b>min points</b> and watch the verdicts
      flip one at a time. Raising min points turns cores into borders, and a
      chain that ran through them dies where they stand.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { arrow, roundRect } from '../../../lib/theorem';

  type P = { x: number; y: number };
  const PALETTE = ['#7c8cff', '#f59e0b', '#2dd4bf', '#f87171', '#a78bfa', '#34d399', '#f472b6', '#38bdf8'];

  const state = { data: 'moons', eps: 42, minPts: 5, running: false };
  let mode: 'clusters' | 'reach' = 'clusters';
  let pts: P[] = [];
  let labels: number[] = [];
  let oi = 0, cid = -1, seeds: number[] = [], done = false;

  const canvas = document.getElementById('db') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const css = (v: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(v).trim();
  const PAD = 44;
  const rnd = (a: number, b: number) => a + Math.random() * (b - a);

  function gen() {
    pts = [];
    if (state.data === 'moons') {
      for (let i = 0; i < 130; i++) {
        const t = Math.PI * (i / 130);
        const r = 190 + rnd(-12, 12);
        pts.push({ x: W / 2 + r * Math.cos(t) - 80, y: H / 2 - r * Math.sin(t) + 55 });
        pts.push({ x: W / 2 + r * Math.cos(t) + 80, y: H / 2 + r * Math.sin(t) - 55 });
      }
    } else {
      const nb = 4;
      const bc = Array.from({ length: nb }, () => ({ x: rnd(PAD + 70, W - PAD - 70), y: rnd(PAD + 70, H - PAD - 70) }));
      for (let i = 0; i < 240; i++) {
        const b = bc[i % nb];
        pts.push({ x: b.x + rnd(-40, 40) + rnd(-14, 14), y: b.y + rnd(-40, 40) + rnd(-14, 14) });
      }
      if (state.data === 'noise')
        for (let i = 0; i < 70; i++) pts.push({ x: rnd(PAD, W - PAD), y: rnd(PAD, H - PAD) });
    }
  }

  function neighbors(i: number) {
    const eps2 = state.eps * state.eps;
    const out: number[] = [];
    for (let j = 0; j < pts.length; j++) {
      if (j === i) continue;
      const dx = pts[i].x - pts[j].x;
      const dy = pts[i].y - pts[j].y;
      if (dx * dx + dy * dy <= eps2) out.push(j);
    }
    return out;
  }

  function restart() {
    labels = new Array(pts.length).fill(-2); // -2 unvisited, -1 noise, >=0 cluster
    oi = 0;
    cid = -1;
    seeds = [];
    done = pts.length === 0;
  }

  function stepOnce() {
    if (seeds.length) {
      const q = seeds.shift()!;
      if (labels[q] === -1) labels[q] = cid; // border reclaimed
      if (labels[q] === -2) {
        labels[q] = cid;
        const nbq = neighbors(q);
        if (nbq.length + 1 >= state.minPts) for (const x of nbq) if (labels[x] < 0) seeds.push(x);
      }
      return;
    }
    while (oi < pts.length && labels[oi] !== -2) oi++;
    if (oi >= pts.length) {
      done = true;
      return;
    }
    const p = oi++;
    const nb = neighbors(p);
    if (nb.length + 1 < state.minPts) {
      labels[p] = -1;
    } else {
      cid++;
      labels[p] = cid;
      seeds = nb.slice();
    }
  }

  function runFull() {
    restart();
    let guard = 0;
    while (!done && guard++ < 200000) stepOnce();
    updateReadout();
  }

  function updateReadout() {
    (document.getElementById('nclust') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(Math.max(0, cid + 1));
    (document.getElementById('nnoise') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(labels.filter((l) => l === -1).length);
  }

  function draw() {
    const ink = css('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);

    const seedSet = new Set(seeds);
    for (let i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {
      const l = labels[i];
      if (l === -2) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink},0.35)`;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.3;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(pts[i].x, pts[i].y, 3.4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.stroke();
      } else {
        ctx.fillStyle = l === -1 ? `rgba(${ink},0.28)` : PALETTE[l % PALETTE.length];
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(pts[i].x, pts[i].y, l === -1 ? 3 : 4.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      if (seedSet.has(i)) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink},0.9)`;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(pts[i].x, pts[i].y, 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }

    // epsilon scale reference
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink},0.5)`;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(40, H - 40, state.eps, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    ctx.fillStyle = css('--text-faint') || '#6b7280';
    ctx.font = "12px 'JetBrains Mono', monospace";
    ctx.fillText('ε', 37, H - 36);
  }

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Reachability and connectivity
  //
  // The clustering above is one long consequence of three relations, and on a
  // few hundred points none of them can be checked by eye. So each case here is
  // a hand-placed handful of points, chosen so that one relation holds and
  // another fails for a reason you can read straight off the picture.
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  type RCase = {
    label: string;
    title: string;
    sub: string;
    eps: number;
    minPts: number;
    pts: P[];
    p: number;
    q: number;
  };

  /** Nine points inside a disc of radius 45: dense at any usable ε. */
  const blob = (cx: number, cy: number): P[] => {
    const out: P[] = [{ x: cx, y: cy }];
    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
      const a = (i * Math.PI) / 3;
      out.push({ x: cx + 45 * Math.cos(a), y: cy + 45 * Math.sin(a) });
    }
    out.push({ x: cx, y: cy - 22 }, { x: cx, y: cy + 22 });
    return out;
  };
  /** A tight seven-point clump, 120 wide, for the two-cluster cases. */
  const clump = (x0: number): P[] => [
    { x: x0, y: 245 }, { x: x0 + 30, y: 215 }, { x: x0 + 30, y: 275 },
    { x: x0 + 60, y: 245 }, { x: x0 + 90, y: 215 }, { x: x0 + 90, y: 275 },
    { x: x0 + 120, y: 245 },
  ];
  /** A chain where every interior point is a core and both ends are borders. */
  const chain: P[] = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => ({
    x: 120 + i * 75,
    y: 245 + 55 * Math.sin(i * 0.75),
  }));

  const CASES: RCase[] = [
    {
      label: 'Both ways',
      title: 'REACHABLE IN BOTH DIRECTIONS',
      sub: 'two cores with a chain of cores between them: the relation runs either way',
      eps: 110, minPts: 3, pts: chain, p: 1, q: 7,
    },
    {
      label: 'One way',
      title: 'REACHABLE ONE WAY ONLY',
      sub: 'a core reaches the border on its fringe, and the border reaches nothing back',
      eps: 100, minPts: 5, pts: [...blob(330, 245), { x: 470, y: 245 }], p: 1, q: 9,
    },
    {
      label: 'Blocked',
      title: 'THE CHAIN STOPS AT A BORDER',
      sub: 'the middle point is reached, but no hop may leave it, so the clusters stay apart',
      eps: 150, minPts: 6, pts: [...clump(200), { x: 465, y: 245 }, ...clump(610)], p: 3, q: 11,
    },
    {
      label: 'Two borders',
      title: 'TWO BORDERS JOINED BY ONE CORE',
      sub: 'neither reaches the other, and they are in one cluster all the same',
      eps: 130, minPts: 5,
      pts: [
        { x: 450, y: 245 }, { x: 425, y: 205 }, { x: 475, y: 205 },
        { x: 425, y: 285 }, { x: 475, y: 285 }, { x: 325, y: 245 }, { x: 575, y: 245 },
      ],
      p: 5, q: 6,
    },
    {
      label: 'Noise',
      title: 'NOISE',
      sub: 'too far to be reached from any core, and too sparse to reach anything',
      eps: 100, minPts: 5, pts: [...blob(330, 245), { x: 700, y: 245 }], p: 0, q: 9,
    },
    {
      label: 'Not core',
      title: 'INSIDE ε IS NOT ENOUGH',
      sub: 'the two are well within ε of each other, and neither is a core, so nothing holds',
      eps: 100, minPts: 5,
      pts: [...blob(250, 245), { x: 600, y: 215 }, { x: 668, y: 260 }], p: 9, q: 10,
    },
  ];

  // clusters here are never drawn in the blue of reachability or the teal of
  // connectivity, so a colour always means one thing
  const RPAL = ['#f59e0b', '#a78bfa', '#f472b6', '#22d3ee'];

  // each case is laid out where its geometry was easiest to reason about, so
  // slide it sideways to sit in the middle of the canvas
  for (const c of CASES) {
    let lo = Infinity, hi = -Infinity;
    for (const q of c.pts) { lo = Math.min(lo, q.x); hi = Math.max(hi, q.x); }
    const dx = 450 - (lo + hi) / 2;
    c.pts = c.pts.map((q) => ({ x: q.x + dx, y: q.y }));
  }

  const rst = { ci: 0, eps: CASES[0].eps, minPts: CASES[0].minPts, p: CASES[0].p, q: CASES[0].q, next: 'q' as 'p' | 'q' };

  const rcanvas = document.getElementById('rc') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const rc = setupCanvas(rcanvas, () => drawReach());
  const rctx = rc.ctx;
  const rink = (a: number) => `rgba(${css('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236'},${a})`;
  const { label: rlabel, textWidth: rwidth } = makeText(rctx, rink);
  const ACC = () => css('--accent') || '#7c8cff';
  const TEAL = () => css('--accent-2') || '#5eead4';
  const BAD = () => css('--danger') || '#f87171';

  type Analysis = {
    c: RCase; N: number[][]; core: boolean[]; lab: number[];
    kind: (i: number) => string;
    direct: (a: number, b: number) => boolean;
    reach: (a: number) => { seen: Set<number>; parent: Map<number, number> };
    path: (a: number, b: number) => number[];
    blocked: (a: number) => boolean;
    witness: number;
  };

  function analyse(): Analysis {
    const c = CASES[rst.ci];
    const pt = c.pts;
    const eps2 = rst.eps * rst.eps;
    const N: number[][] = pt.map((_, i) =>
      pt.map((_, j) => j).filter((j) => {
        if (j === i) return false;
        const dx = pt[i].x - pt[j].x, dy = pt[i].y - pt[j].y;
        return dx * dx + dy * dy <= eps2;
      })
    );
    const core = N.map((l) => l.length + 1 >= rst.minPts);

    // the clusters themselves, so a case can show that two points share one
    const lab: number[] = new Array(pt.length).fill(-2);
    let cc = -1;
    for (let i = 0; i < pt.length; i++) {
      if (lab[i] !== -2) continue;
      if (!core[i]) { lab[i] = -1; continue; }
      cc++;
      lab[i] = cc;
      const sd = N[i].slice();
      while (sd.length) {
        const u = sd.shift()!;
        if (lab[u] === -1) lab[u] = cc;
        if (lab[u] === -2) {
          lab[u] = cc;
          if (core[u]) for (const v of N[u]) if (lab[v] < 0) sd.push(v);
        }
      }
    }

    const reach = (a: number) => {
      const parent = new Map<number, number>();
      const seen = new Set<number>([a]);
      const queue: number[] = core[a] ? [a] : [];
      while (queue.length) {
        const u = queue.shift()!;
        for (const v of N[u])
          if (!seen.has(v)) {
            seen.add(v);
            parent.set(v, u);
            if (core[v]) queue.push(v);
          }
      }
      return { seen, parent };
    };
    const path = (a: number, b: number) => {
      const r = reach(a);
      if (!r.seen.has(b) || a === b) return [];
      const out = [b];
      let cur = b;
      while (r.parent.has(cur)) { cur = r.parent.get(cur)!; out.push(cur); }
      return out.reverse();
    };
    const direct = (a: number, b: number) => {
      if (a === b || !core[a]) return false;
      const dx = pt[a].x - pt[b].x, dy = pt[a].y - pt[b].y;
      return dx * dx + dy * dy <= eps2;
    };
    // a chain that ends at a border with a neighbour outside: the hop it would
    // need to make is exactly the one the definition forbids
    const blocked = (a: number) => {
      const r = reach(a);
      for (const m of r.seen)
        if (m !== a && !core[m] && N[m].some((v) => !r.seen.has(v))) return true;
      return false;
    };

    let witness = -1;
    let best = Infinity;
    for (let o = 0; o < pt.length; o++) {
      if (!core[o]) continue;
      const r = reach(o);
      if (!r.seen.has(rst.p) || !r.seen.has(rst.q)) continue;
      const cost = path(o, rst.p).length + path(o, rst.q).length;
      if (cost < best) { best = cost; witness = o; }
    }

    const kind = (i: number) => (core[i] ? 'core' : lab[i] >= 0 ? 'border' : 'noise');
    return { c, N, core, lab, kind, direct, reach, path, blocked, witness };
  }

  const dist = (a: P, b: P) => Math.hypot(a.x - b.x, a.y - b.y);

  function hop(a: P, b: P, colour: string, lw = 2) {
    const d = dist(a, b) || 1;
    const ux = (b.x - a.x) / d, uy = (b.y - a.y) / d;
    arrow(rctx, a.x + ux * 10, a.y + uy * 10, b.x - ux * 12, b.y - uy * 12, colour, lw, 8);
  }

  function drawReach() {
    const A = analyse();
    const c = A.c;
    const pt = c.pts;
    const RW = rc.W, RH = rc.H;
    const acc = ACC(), teal = TEAL(), bad = BAD();
    rctx.clearRect(0, 0, RW, RH);

    rlabel(c.title, 60, 46, 0.75, 'left', 13, acc);
    rlabel(c.sub, 60, 66, 0.34, 'left', 11);

    const Rp = A.reach(rst.p);
    const pathPQ = A.path(rst.p, rst.q);
    const pathQP = A.path(rst.q, rst.p);
    const connected = A.witness >= 0;

    // everything p can reach, as a soft halo
    rctx.fillStyle = acc;
    rctx.globalAlpha = 0.36;
    for (const i of Rp.seen) {
      rctx.beginPath();
      rctx.arc(pt[i].x, pt[i].y, 15, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      rctx.fill();
    }
    rctx.globalAlpha = 1;

    // the ε that the two points under discussion actually see
    rctx.setLineDash([4, 5]);
    rctx.lineWidth = 1.2;
    for (const i of [rst.p, rst.q]) {
      rctx.strokeStyle = rink(0.26);
      rctx.beginPath();
      rctx.arc(pt[i].x, pt[i].y, rst.eps, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      rctx.stroke();
    }
    rctx.setLineDash([]);

    // the chain, when there is one, or else the two chains that connect them
    if (pathPQ.length > 1) for (let i = 0; i < pathPQ.length - 1; i++) hop(pt[pathPQ[i]], pt[pathPQ[i + 1]], acc, 2.2);
    else if (pathQP.length > 1) for (let i = 0; i < pathQP.length - 1; i++) hop(pt[pathQP[i]], pt[pathQP[i + 1]], acc, 2.2);
    else if (connected) {
      for (const t of [rst.p, rst.q]) {
        const pa = A.path(A.witness, t);
        for (let i = 0; i < pa.length - 1; i++) hop(pt[pa[i]], pt[pa[i + 1]], teal, 2);
      }
    }

    // the points, drawn as what they are
    for (let i = 0; i < pt.length; i++) {
      const k = A.kind(i);
      const col = A.lab[i] >= 0 ? RPAL[A.lab[i] % RPAL.length] : rink(0.34);
      if (k === 'core') {
        rctx.fillStyle = col;
        rctx.beginPath();
        rctx.arc(pt[i].x, pt[i].y, 6.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        rctx.fill();
      } else if (k === 'border') {
        rctx.strokeStyle = col;
        rctx.lineWidth = 2;
        rctx.beginPath();
        rctx.arc(pt[i].x, pt[i].y, 5.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        rctx.stroke();
      } else {
        rctx.fillStyle = rink(0.34);
        rctx.beginPath();
        rctx.arc(pt[i].x, pt[i].y, 3.4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        rctx.fill();
      }
    }

    // p, q and the core that connects them
    const mark = (i: number, name: string, colour: string, below = false) => {
      rctx.strokeStyle = colour;
      rctx.lineWidth = 1.8;
      rctx.beginPath();
      rctx.arc(pt[i].x, pt[i].y, 13, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      rctx.stroke();
      const t = `${name} · ${A.kind(i)}`;
      const cy = pt[i].y + (below ? 36 : -28);
      const w = rwidth(t, 11.5) + 16;
      rctx.fillStyle = css('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
      rctx.globalAlpha = 0.92;
      roundRect(rctx, pt[i].x - w / 2, cy - 11, w, 20, 6);
      rctx.fill();
      rctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      rctx.strokeStyle = rink(0.16);
      rctx.lineWidth = 1;
      rctx.stroke();
      rlabel(t, pt[i].x, cy + 4, 0.9, 'center', 11.5, colour);
    };
    if (connected && pathPQ.length < 2 && pathQP.length < 2 && A.witness !== rst.p && A.witness !== rst.q)
      mark(A.witness, 'o', teal);
    mark(rst.p, 'p', rink(0.9));
    mark(rst.q, 'q', rink(0.9), true);

    // legend
    const ly = 384;
    rctx.fillStyle = rink(0.75);
    rctx.beginPath(); rctx.arc(66, ly - 4, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2); rctx.fill();
    rlabel('core', 78, ly, 0.4, 'left', 11);
    rctx.strokeStyle = rink(0.6); rctx.lineWidth = 2;
    rctx.beginPath(); rctx.arc(146, ly - 4, 5.5, 0, Math.PI * 2); rctx.stroke();
    rlabel('border', 158, ly, 0.4, 'left', 11);
    rctx.fillStyle = rink(0.34);
    rctx.beginPath(); rctx.arc(240, ly - 4, 3.4, 0, Math.PI * 2); rctx.fill();
    rlabel('noise', 252, ly, 0.4, 'left', 11);
    rlabel('dashed circle = ε · shaded = everything p reaches', 340, ly, 0.3, 'left', 11);

    drawCard(A, pathPQ, pathQP, connected);
  }

  /** The five verdicts, each with the reason it came out that way. */
  function drawCard(A: Analysis, pathPQ: number[], pathQP: number[], connected: boolean) {
    const pt = A.c.pts;
    const teal = TEAL(), bad = BAD();
    const x0 = 60, x1 = 840, y0 = 410;
    rctx.fillStyle = rink(0.03);
    roundRect(rctx, x0, y0, x1 - x0, 218, 10);
    rctx.fill();
    rctx.strokeStyle = rink(0.12);
    rctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rctx.stroke();

    rlabel('core: minPts points within ε, itself included', x0 + 26, y0 + 28, 0.42, 'left', 11);
    rlabel('→ direct · ⇒ chain · ↔ connected', x1 - 26, y0 + 28, 0.42, 'right', 11);
    rctx.strokeStyle = rink(0.1);
    rctx.beginPath();
    rctx.moveTo(x0 + 20, y0 + 44);
    rctx.lineTo(x1 - 20, y0 + 44);
    rctx.stroke();

    const d = dist(pt[rst.p], pt[rst.q]);
    const dtxt = `d = ${Math.round(d)}`;
    const directWhy = (a: number, b: number, an: string) =>
      A.direct(a, b)
        ? `${an} is a core and ${dtxt} ≤ ε`
        : !A.core[a]
          ? d <= rst.eps
            ? `${an} is not a core, even though ${dtxt} ≤ ε`
            : `${an} is not a core point`
          : `${dtxt} > ε = ${rst.eps}`;
    const reachWhy = (a: number, b: number, an: string, path: number[]) =>
      path.length > 1
        ? `${path.length - 1} hop${path.length > 2 ? 's' : ''}, every one of them leaving a core`
        : !A.core[a]
          ? `${an} is not a core, so no chain can leave it`
          : A.blocked(a)
            ? 'the chain is stopped at a border point'
            : 'no chain of cores gets there';

    const rows: [string, string, boolean, string][] = [
      ['p → q', 'directly reachable', A.direct(rst.p, rst.q), directWhy(rst.p, rst.q, 'p')],
      ['q → p', 'directly reachable', A.direct(rst.q, rst.p), directWhy(rst.q, rst.p, 'q')],
      ['p ⇒ q', 'reachable', pathPQ.length > 1, reachWhy(rst.p, rst.q, 'p', pathPQ)],
      ['q ⇒ p', 'reachable', pathQP.length > 1, reachWhy(rst.q, rst.p, 'q', pathQP)],
      [
        'p ↔ q', 'connected', connected,
        connected
          ? A.witness === rst.p || A.witness === rst.q
            ? 'one of them is itself the core that reaches both'
            : 'the core marked o reaches both of them'
          : A.core[rst.p] || A.core[rst.q]
            ? 'no single core reaches both'
            : 'neither of them is reached from any core',
      ],
    ];

    rows.forEach(([sym, name, ok, why], i) => {
      const y = y0 + 78 + i * 32;
      rlabel(sym, x0 + 26, y, 0.85, 'left', 13);
      rlabel(name, x0 + 116, y, 0.55, 'left', 11.5);
      rlabel(ok ? 'yes' : 'no', x0 + 300, y, 1, 'left', 12.5, ok ? teal : bad);
      rlabel(why, x0 + 348, y, 0.38, 'left', 11);
    });
  }

  function syncReachPanel() {
    const A = analyse();
    (document.getElementById('pkind') as HTMLElement).textContent = A.kind(rst.p);
    (document.getElementById('qkind') as HTMLElement).textContent = A.kind(rst.q);
    (document.getElementById('samec') as HTMLElement).textContent =
      A.lab[rst.p] >= 0 && A.lab[rst.p] === A.lab[rst.q] ? 'yes' : 'no';
    (document.getElementById('nextsel') as HTMLElement).textContent = rst.next;
  }

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // wiring
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const epsEl = document.getElementById('eps') as HTMLInputElement;
  const mpEl = document.getElementById('mp') as HTMLInputElement;
  const runBtn = document.getElementById('run') as HTMLButtonElement;

  const NOTES = {
    clusters:
      'Click the canvas to add points. Restart, then Step, to watch clusters flood outward from dense cores.',
    reach:
      'Click any point to move q, then p, and read the five verdicts. Each case brings its own ε and min points; drag either slider to break the case and watch which line flips first.',
  };

  function showMode() {
    const cl = mode === 'clusters';
    canvas.hidden = !cl;
    rcanvas.hidden = cl;
    el('cl-controls').hidden = !cl;
    el('rc-controls').hidden = cl;
    el('cl-readout').hidden = !cl;
    el('rc-readout').hidden = cl;
    el('note').textContent = cl ? NOTES.clusters : NOTES.reach;
    const eps = cl ? state.eps : rst.eps;
    const mp = cl ? state.minPts : rst.minPts;
    // the two views work at different scales, so the slider keeps its own range
    epsEl.min = cl ? '12' : '40';
    epsEl.max = cl ? '90' : '200';
    epsEl.value = String(eps);
    mpEl.value = String(mp);
    el('epsval').textContent = String(eps);
    el('mpval').textContent = String(mp);
    if (!cl) syncReachPanel();
  }

  function loadCase(i: number) {
    rst.ci = i;
    rst.eps = CASES[i].eps;
    rst.minPts = CASES[i].minPts;
    rst.p = CASES[i].p;
    rst.q = CASES[i].q;
    rst.next = 'q';
    showMode();
  }

  el('mode').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    el('mode').querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    mode = btn.dataset.m as 'clusters' | 'reach';
    state.running = false;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Run';
    showMode();
  });

  el('rcase').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    el('rcase').querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    loadCase(+btn.dataset.c!);
  });

  el('data').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    el('data').querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.data = btn.dataset.d!;
    gen();
    runFull();
  });

  epsEl.addEventListener('input', () => {
    el('epsval').textContent = epsEl.value;
    if (mode === 'clusters') {
      state.eps = +epsEl.value;
      runFull();
    } else {
      rst.eps = +epsEl.value;
      syncReachPanel();
    }
  });
  mpEl.addEventListener('input', () => {
    el('mpval').textContent = mpEl.value;
    if (mode === 'clusters') {
      state.minPts = +mpEl.value;
      runFull();
    } else {
      rst.minPts = +mpEl.value;
      syncReachPanel();
    }
  });

  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (mode !== 'clusters') return;
    if (done) restart();
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('step').addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (mode !== 'clusters') return;
    if (done) restart();
    stepOnce();
    updateReadout();
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (mode !== 'clusters') return;
    state.running = false;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Run';
    restart();
    updateReadout();
  });
  el('regen').addEventListener('click', () => {
    gen();
    runFull();
  });
  el('clear').addEventListener('click', () => {
    pts = [];
    state.running = false;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Run';
    restart();
    updateReadout();
  });

  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    pts.push({
      x: ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * W,
      y: ((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * H,
    });
    runFull();
  });

  const rcAt = (e: PointerEvent | MouseEvent) => {
    const rect = rcanvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    const x = ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * rc.W;
    const y = ((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * rc.H;
    const pt = CASES[rst.ci].pts;
    let best = -1, bd = 24;
    for (let i = 0; i < pt.length; i++) {
      const d = dist(pt[i], { x, y });
      if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; }
    }
    return best;
  };

  rcanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    const i = rcAt(e);
    if (i < 0 || i === rst.p || i === rst.q) return;
    if (rst.next === 'q') { rst.q = i; rst.next = 'p'; } else { rst.p = i; rst.next = 'q'; }
    syncReachPanel();
  });
  rcanvas.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
    rcanvas.style.cursor = rcAt(e) >= 0 ? 'pointer' : 'default';
  });

  function loop() {
    if (mode === 'clusters') {
      if (state.running) {
        for (let k = 0; k < 6 && !done; k++) stepOnce();
        updateReadout();
        if (done) {
          state.running = false;
          runBtn.textContent = 'Run';
        }
      }
      draw();
    } else {
      drawReach();
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(loop);
  }

  gen();
  runFull();
  showMode();
  requestAnimationFrame(loop);
</script>

<style>
  /* Both views live in the same stage, so the hidden one has to lose the
     display:block that .sim-stage canvas hands it. */
  .sim-stage canvas[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  #cl-controls,
  #rc-controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  #cl-controls[hidden],
  #rc-controls[hidden],
  .readout[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
